[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Caro-Kann Defence: Advance Variation"]
[Variation "Short Variation"]
[ECO "B12"]
[Character "solid,positional"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "pawn-chain,c5-break"]
[For "white"]
[Kind "main"]
[Opponent "3...Bf5"]
[Start "1. e4"]

1... c6 { Prepares ...d5 with a pawn behind it, so the centre pawn is always defended. Black gets a solid centre without shutting in the c8 bishop. } 2. d4 d5 { Challenges the pawn on e4. The c6 pawn guards d5, so Black can recapture there with a pawn. } 3. e5 { Gains space. The pawn on e5 takes squares from Black's knight and cannot easily be attacked. } 3... Bf5 { Brings the bishop out before ...e6 closes its diagonal. This is the whole point of the Caro-Kann: Black never ends up with a bad bishop. } 4. Nf3 { Develops and guards d4, the pawn at the base of White's chain. [%csl Gd4] } 4... e6 { With the bishop safely outside the pawn chain, ...e6 can support d5. } 5. Be2 { Safe and quiet, and it clears the way to castle. On d3 the bishop could be traded off by ...Bxd3. } 5... c5 { Attacks the base of White's pawn chain at d4. If that pawn goes, the pawn on e5 loses its support. } 6. O-O { Castle first. Next comes c3 to guard d4 twice, and then Nbd2. } 6... Nc6 ( 6... Qb6 $6 { Black eyes b2 and d4 together, but it spends a move while White is ready to strike. } 7. c4 { Opens the centre before Black is developed. The queen is out on b6 and the bishop on c1 still guards b2. } 7... Nc6 8. cxd5 exd5 9. Nc3 { Piles up on d5 and d4; Black's queen has no good square. } 9... Qd8 10. Bg5 Be7 11. Nb5 ) ( 6... cxd4 7. Nxd4 { The knight recaptures with a threat on the bishop. } 7... Bg6 8. c4 { Hits d5 and takes more space; Black's pieces are cramped. } 8... dxc4 9. Qa4+ Nd7 10. Be3 ) 7. c3 { Now d4 is guarded twice, by the knight and the pawn. Count the guards before anyone captures there. [%csl Gd4] } 7... cxd4 ( 7... Bg4 8. Nbd2 { Brings the last piece out and covers d4 again. } 8... cxd4 9. cxd4 a5 10. h3 { Asks the bishop what it wants to do before it can take on f3. } 10... Bh5 11. Qb3 ) 8. cxd4 Nge7 9. Nc3 { The knight adds a third defender to d4 and eyes b5 and d5. } 9... Bg4 10. Nd2 { Steps away so that ...Bxf3 cannot spoil the pawns. The knight comes back to f3 after the bishops trade. } 10... Bxe2 11. Nxe2 Nf5 12. Nf3 Rc8 { White has more space and a solid pawn chain. If Black leaves the book, castle, guard d4 and play Rb1 and b4 to grow on the queenside. } *
